    <snippet id="run-qodana">

        <link-summary>Basic examples of running %product%.</link-summary>

        <note><include from="lib_qd.topic" element-id="docker-ram-note"/></note>

        <include from="lib_qd.topic" element-id="root-and-non-root-users-info-bubble"/>

        <p filter="ruby">You can run %product% using available Docker images.</p>

        <p filter="non-ruby">You can run %product% linters using the following methods:</p>
        <list filter="non-ruby">
          <li filter="native"><a href="deploy-qodana.md" anchor="deploy-qodana-native-mode">Native mode</a> as the recommended method for running
            linters without Docker</li>
          <li>Docker mode using Docker containers of %product%</li>
            <li><a href="qodana-ide-plugin.md">%ide%</a></li>
        </list>

        <tabs group="native-container" filter="non-ruby">
            <tab title="Native mode" group-key="native-mode" filter="native">
                <tabs group="software">
                    <tab title="GitHub Actions" group-key="github">
                        <p>You can run %product% using the <a href="https://github.com/marketplace/actions/qodana-scan">Qodana Scan GitHub action</a>.</p>
                        <p>To analyze the <code>main</code> branch, release branches and the pull requests coming
                            to your repository in native mode, save this workflow configuration to the <code>.github/workflows/code_quality.yml</code> file:</p>
                        <code-block lang="yaml" filter="generic">
                            name: Qodana
                            on:
                                workflow_dispatch:
                                pull_request:
                                push:
                                    branches: # Specify your branches here
                                        - main # The 'main' branch
                                        - 'releases/*' # The release branches
                            jobs:
                                qodana:
                                    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
                                    permissions:
                                        contents: write
                                        pull-requests: write
                                        checks: write
                                    steps:
                                        - uses: actions/checkout@v3
                                          with:
                                              ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}  # to check out the actual pull request commit, not the merge commit
                                              fetch-depth: 0  # a full history is required for pull request analysis
                                        - name: 'Qodana Scan'
                                          uses: %action-version%
                                          with:
                                              args: |
                                                  --linter %qd-linter%
                                                  --within-docker false
                                          env:
                                              QODANA_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.QODANA_TOKEN }}
                        </code-block>
                        <code-block lang="yaml" filter="python">
                            name: Qodana
                            on:
                                workflow_dispatch:
                                pull_request:
                                push:
                                    branches: # Specify your branches here
                                        - main # The 'main' branch
                                        - 'releases/*' # The release branches
                            jobs:
                                qodana:
                                    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
                                    permissions:
                                        contents: write
                                        pull-requests: write
                                        checks: write
                                    steps:
                                        - uses: actions/checkout@v3
                                          with:
                                              ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}  # to check out the actual pull request commit, not the merge commit
                                              fetch-depth: 0  # a full history is required for pull request analysis
                                        - name: 'Qodana Scan'
                                          uses: %action-version%
                                          with:
                                              args: |
                                                  --linter %qd-linter-combined%
                                                  --within-docker false
                                          env:
                                              QODANA_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.QODANA_TOKEN }}
                        </code-block>
                        <code-block lang="yaml" filter="jvm">
                            name: Qodana
                            on:
                                workflow_dispatch:
                                pull_request:
                                push:
                                    branches: # Specify your branches here
                                        - main # The 'main' branch
                                        - 'releases/*' # The release branches
                            jobs:
                                qodana:
                                    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
                                    permissions:
                                        contents: write
                                        pull-requests: write
                                        checks: write
                                    steps:
                                        - uses: actions/checkout@v3
                                          with:
                                              ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}  # to check out the actual pull request commit, not the merge commit
                                              fetch-depth: 0  # a full history is required for pull request analysis
                                        - name: 'Qodana Scan'
                                          uses: %action-version%
                                          with:
                                              args: |
                                                  --linter %qd-linter-combined%
                                                  --within-docker false
                                          env:
                                              QODANA_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.QODANA_TOKEN }}
                        </code-block>
                        <p>This configuration uses the <code>--linter</code>
                            <a href="docker-image-configuration.topic" anchor="docker-config-reference-qodana-scan">option</a>
                            to specify a <a href="linters.md">linter</a>. The
                            <code>--within-docker</code> option in the <code>false</code> state is used for enabling native mode.</p>
                        <p filter="jvm">To manage access to private Maven repositories, do the following:</p>
                        <procedure filter="jvm">
                            <step>
                                <p>Create the <code>settings.xml</code> file containing references to credentials of your private Maven repository, for example:</p>
                                <code-block lang="xml" filter="jvm">
                                    &lt;servers&gt;
                                        &lt;server&gt;
                                            &lt;id&gt;my-secret-repository&lt;/id&gt;
                                            &lt;username&gt;${env.REPOSITORY_USERNAME}&lt;/username&gt;
                                            &lt;password&gt;${env.REPOSITORY_PASSWORD}&lt;/password&gt;
                                        &lt;/server&gt;
                                    &lt;/servers&gt;
                                </code-block>
                            </step>
                            <step>
                                <p>In your GitHub Actions configuration, create the <code>~/.m2/</code> directory, and copy the <code>settings.xml</code> file there, for example:</p>
                                <code-block lang="yaml" filter="jvm">
                                      - uses: actions/setup-java@v4
                                        with:
                                            settings-path: ${{ github.workspace }}

                                      - name: Place Maven settings.xml where %product% expects it
                                        run: |
                                            mkdir -p ~/.m2
                                            cp "${{ github.workspace }}/settings.xml" ~/.m2/settings.xml
                                </code-block>
                            </step>
                            <step><p>In your GitHub Actions configuration, export the credentials values to the environment variables, for example:</p>
                                <code-block lang="yaml" filter="jvm">
                                  - name: Qodana Scan
                                    uses: %action-version%
                                    env:
                                        QODANA_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.QODANA_TOKEN }}
                                        REPOSITORY_USERNAME: ${{ secrets.REPOSITORY_USERNAME }}
                                        REPOSITORY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.REPOSITORY_PASSWORD }}
                                </code-block>
                            </step>
                        </procedure>
                        <p>More configuration examples are available in the <a href="github.md"/> section.</p>
                    </tab>
                    <tab title="Command line" group-key="command-line">
                        <p>Run this command in the project root directory:</p>
                        <code-block lang="shell" prompt="$" filter="generic">
                            qodana scan \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-e QODANA_TOKEN="&lt;qodana-cloud-token&gt;" \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--linter %qd-linter% \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--within-docker false
                        </code-block>
                        <code-block lang="shell" prompt="$" filter="python">
                            qodana scan \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-e QODANA_TOKEN="&lt;qodana-cloud-token&gt;" \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--linter %qd-linter-combined% \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--within-docker false
                        </code-block>
                        <code-block lang="shell" prompt="$" filter="jvm">
                            qodana scan \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-e QODANA_TOKEN="&lt;qodana-cloud-token&gt;" \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--linter %qd-linter-combined% \
                            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--within-docker false
                        </code-block>
                        <p>This configuration uses the <code>--linter</code>
                            <a href="docker-image-configuration.topic" anchor="docker-config-reference-qodana-scan">option</a>
                            to specify a <a href="linters.md">linter</a>. The
                            <code>--within-docker</code> option in the <code>false</code> state is used for enabling native mode.</p>
                        <p>If you are using another %cloud% instance than https://qodana.cloud/, override it by declaring the <code>QODANA_ENDPOINT</code> environment variable.</p>
                        <p>In your browser, open <a href="https://qodana.cloud">%cloud%</a> to examine analysis reports and
                            reconfigure the analysis. See the <a href="ui-overview.md"/> section of the documentation for full details.</p>
                    </tab>
                </tabs>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Docker mode" group-key="container-mode">
                <p filter="native">Docker mode is available for all linters; however, it is advised that you use native mode whenever possible.</p>
                <note id="major-version-note">The configured major version of a %product% linter (<ui-path>20**.*</ui-path>) should match the version specified
                        in the <a href="qodana-yaml.md">qodana.yaml</a> file.</note>
                <include from="lib_qd.topic" element-id="run-qodana-container-mode-config-examples"/>
            </tab>
            <tab title="%ide%" group-key="ides" filter="non-ruby">
                <procedure>
                    <step>
                        <p>In %ide%, navigate to <ui-path>Tools | Qodana | Try Code Analysis with Qodana</ui-path>.</p>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>On the <ui-path>Run Qodana</ui-path> dialog, you can configure %product%.</p>
                        <img src="ide-plugin-run-qodana-2.png" width="793" alt="Configuring Qodana in the Run Qodana dialog" border-effect="line"/>
                        <p>This dialog contains the following components:</p>
                        <table>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Name</td>
                                <td>Description</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>The <code>qodana.yaml</code> file</td>
                                <td>In the text field, you can set up code analysis used by Qodana in this file. You can learn more about available <a href="qodana-yaml.md">configuration options</a></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>The <ui-path>Send analysis results to %cloud%</ui-path> option</td>
                                <td>If you want to send reports to %cloud%, you can check this option and paste the <a href="project-token.md">project token</a> generated in <a href="cloud-projects.topic" anchor="cloud-manage-projects">%cloud%</a></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>The <ui-path>Save qodana.yaml in project root</ui-path> option</td>
                                <td>By checking this option, you can save the %product% configuration made on this dialog to the <a href="qodana-yaml.md"><code>qodana.yaml</code></a> file in the project root of your project</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>The <ui-path>Use Qodana analysis baseline</ui-path> option</td>
                                <td>Using the <a href="baseline.topic">baseline</a> feature, you can skip analysis for specific problems</td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                        <p>Click <ui-path>Run</ui-path> to analyze your code.</p>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>On the <ui-path>Qodana</ui-path> tab of the <ui-path>Problems</ui-path> tool window, see the <a href="qodana-ide-plugin.md" anchor="ide-plugin-study-reports">analysis report</a>.</p>
                    </step>
                </procedure>
            </tab>
        </tabs>
    </snippet>

