    <snippet id="explore-analysis-results">

        <tabs group="software">
            <tab title="%ide%" group-key="ides">
                <p>You can load the latest %instance% report from %cloud% to %ide% as explained below.</p>
                <procedure>
                    <step>
                        <p>In %ide%, navigate to <ui-path>Tools | Qodana | Log in to Qodana</ui-path>.</p>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>
                            On the <ui-path>Settings</ui-path> dialog, click <ui-path>Log in</ui-path>.
                        </p>
                        <img src="ide-plugin-connect-1.png" dark-src="ide-plugin-connect-1_dark.png" width="706" alt="Connecting to %cloud%" border-effect="line"/>
                        <p>This will redirect you to the authentication page.</p>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>Select the <a href="cloud-projects.topic">%cloud% project</a> to link your local project with.</p>
                        <img src="ide-plugin-connect-2.png" dark-src="ide-plugin-connect-2_dark.png" width="706" alt="Linking the project to %cloud%" border-effect="line"/>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>If you check the <ui-path>Always load most relevant Qodana report</ui-path> option, you will
                            be able to receive the most actual and relevant reports from %cloud%.</p>
                        <img src="ide-plugin-connect-3.png" dark-src="ide-plugin-connect-3_dark.png" width="706" alt="Enabling to load the most relevant reports" border-effect="line"/>
                        <p>In this case, the IDE will search %cloud% and fetch the report with the revision ID
                            corresponding to the current revision ID (HEAD). If this report is not found, the IDE will
                            select the previous report with the revision ID closest to the current revision ID (HEAD).
                            Otherwise, the IDE retrieves the latest available report from %cloud%.</p>
                    </step>
                    <step>
                        <p>On the <ui-path>Qodana</ui-path> tab of the <ui-path>Problems</ui-path> tool
                            window, see the <a href="qodana-ide-plugin.md" anchor="ide-plugin-study-reports">analysis report</a>.</p>
                    </step>
                </procedure>
            </tab>
            <tab title="%cloud%" group-key="cloud">
                <include from="lib_qd.topic" element-id="explore-analysis-results-qodana-cloud"/>
            </tab>
        </tabs>

